factory: qa PASS refused, nothing recorded: gate b exit=1; gate c exit=unknown
Gate line format: `- <name> exit=<code> cmd=<command>`, one per line under a line `## Gates`, e.g.
## Gates
- unittest exit=0 cmd=python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
- compile exit=0 cmd=python3 -m py_compile bin/factory
Gates are commands that must succeed (suite, build, lint); a check whose correct result is a non-zero exit belongs in the per-criterion list instead.
